Ladybird synthesizes bold for a bold request to a face whose own
font-weight descriptor stops below 600, whatever its file holds, and
goes by the font’s weight axis only for a face with no descriptor.
Each engine does the same: Blink’s CSSSegmentedFontFace::GetFontData()
sets synthetic bold from the face’s FontSelectionCapabilities, and its
FontCustomPlatformData::GetFontPlatformData() reads the wght axis only
when those capabilities came from auto. WebKit’s CSSSegmentedFontFace
sets it from selectionCapabilities.weight.maximum. And in Gecko, the
gfxFontEntry::SupportsBold() check reads the descriptor’s maximum
weight, and reads the weight axis only for an auto-weight user font.
